                           "This is **bold** and _italic_!\n"
                           "Check out this [ ] checkbox\n\n"
                           "`code block in single ticks`\n"
                           "\n"
                           "| left | right |\n"
                           "|------|-------|\n"
                           "| one  | two   |\n";

    std::cout << convertMarkdownToHTML(markdown) << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
``` 

Note that this implementation supports only basic Markdown formatting such as headings, bold, italic, checkboxes, fenced code blocks with `\n`, and simple tables. For more advanced features such as links, images, lists etc., you'll likely need additional parsing logic and HTML output. Also note that this implementation assumes UTF-8 encoding both for Markdown input and generated HTML output strings.

