Problem Statement:

Given an array of n integers, find the maximum sum of non-overlapping contiguous subarrays with length exactly k.

Examples:

1. Input: [4, -2, 5, -3, 7], k = 3
   Output: 19
   Subarrays with required lengths: (4), (-2, 5), (-3, 7)

2. Input: [-6, 7, -9, 5, 8], k = 2
   Output: 17
   Subarrays with required lengths: (-6, 7), (5, 8)

Constraints:
- The input array contains only integer values.
- 2 <= n <= 10^5
- 2 <= k <= n

Solution Approach:
This problem can be solved using dynamic programming. Let dp[i][j] represent the maximum sum obtained by choosing j out of first i elements for prefix length j (i.e., a subarray ending at index I-1 of length j). We will fill up dp[][] in a bottom-up fashion.

For subproblems where j < k or I-j >= k (meaning there are not enough elements to form a subarray of length k), we simply take the maximum value among no selection, selecting only one element, or taking two adjacent elements if possible. Otherwise, we take the maximum value between considering the last element alone and adding the (k-1)-th last element of a larger subarray of length k selected from the remaining elements (prefix).

```
// Java code to solve the above-proposed Problem

public class MaxSumNonOverlappingSubarray {
    public static int maxSumNonOverlap(int[] arr, int k) {
        int n = arr.length;
        int[][] dp = new int[n+1][n+1]; // 0-indexed array

        // base case
        for (int I = 1; I <= n; i++) {
            dp[i][1] = Math.max(arr[i-1], 0);
        }

        // fill up dp[][] table in a bottom-up manner
        for (int I = k+1; I <= n; i++) {
            for (int j = 2; j <= k; j++) {
                dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-k][j-1]);
            }
        }

        for (int I = k+1; I <= n; i++) {
            dp[i][k] = arr[i-1];
            for (int j = k-1; j >= 2; j--) {
                int r = i - k + j;
                dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[r][j-1] + arr[i-1],
                        Math.max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-k][j-1]));
            }
        }

        // Find the optimal solution
        int res = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int I = k; I <= n; i++) {
            res = Math.max(res, dp[i][k]);
        }

        return res;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {4, -2, 5, -3, 7};
        int k = 3;

        System.out.println("Maximum Sum for non-overlapping subarrays of size " + k + ": " +
                maxSumNonOverlap(arr, k));

        // Test cases
        int[] testCases = {{-6, 7, -9, 5, 8}, {7, 2, -7, 11}, {-1, -2, -3, -4}};
        int expectedValues = {17, 22, -15};

        for (int I = 0; I < testCases.length; i++) {
            assertEquals(expectedValues[i], maxSumNonOverlap(testCases[i], 2));
        }
    }
}
``` 

Time Complexity: O(n*k)
Space Complexity: O(n*k)user

